From 59699915f41851c7bcc65636a78e3171c86f21f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] avalanche: add treasury contender voting, 50/25/25 reward
 split, and default slate

Add on-chain Avalanche treasury contender voting (avatreasury), enforce
the 50/25/25 Miner/Staker/Treasury coinbase split, and configure the default slate.

Original-Commit: 07e3d8ee05e71a2e7587895f853798a8025aa986
Original-Patch: v2/022
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Retain original native treasury consensus/voting and native state-anchor replacement while preserving shared mempool-batch variant, conflict finalization and visitor behavior. Reconcile inventory-kind handling with native inbound flag and retain actual TxId inventory. State-anchor removal follows original native header-root adapter; authentication parity remains an explicit113 audit item.
(cherry picked from commit 04e0deb7f117b175da6a6a4ce241f42fed670747)

Canonical-Source-Commit: 04e0deb7f117b175da6a6a4ce241f42fed670747

T1 native adaptation: treasury removes legacy StateAnchor support, so retain batch capability gates, positive controls and ordinary poll coverage while removing only unsupported StateAnchor test assertions and arguments.
